{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-15177","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14011","text":"Skill 08 — Provider Implementation"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-15179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14012","text":"How to build a provider that satisfies a [&] Protocol capability contract. Registration, conformance testing, and MCP transport binding."}]}],"id":"blk-15178","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-15180","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14013","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15181","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14014","text":"Why This Matters"}]},{"id":"blk-15182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14015","text":"Capabilities are interfaces. Providers are implementations. The protocol is only as useful as the providers that satisfy its contracts. This file teaches you how to build one."}]},{"id":"blk-15183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14016","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15184","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14017","text":"The Provider Concept"}]},{"id":"blk-15185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14018","text":"A provider is a service that implements one or more capability contracts. The [&] Protocol ecosystem includes default providers:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-15187","spans":[{"id":"spn-14019","text":"Provider"}]},{"id":"blk-15188","spans":[{"id":"spn-14020","text":"Capabilities Provided"}]}],"id":"blk-15186","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-15189","spans":[{"id":"spn-14021","text":"Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-15190","spans":[{"id":"spn-14022","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-14023","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14024","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.episodic"},{"id":"spn-14025","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14026","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-14027","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14028","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.attend"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15191","spans":[{"id":"spn-14029","text":"TickTickClock"}]},{"id":"blk-15192","spans":[{"id":"spn-14030","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-14031","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14032","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.forecast"},{"id":"spn-14033","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14034","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.pattern"},{"id":"spn-14035","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14036","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.baseline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15193","spans":[{"id":"spn-14037","text":"GeoFleetic"}]},{"id":"blk-15194","spans":[{"id":"spn-14038","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.fleet"},{"id":"spn-14039","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14040","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.geofence"},{"id":"spn-14041","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14042","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.route"},{"id":"spn-14043","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14044","marks":["code"],"text":"&space.region"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15195","spans":[{"id":"spn-14045","text":"Deliberatic"}]},{"id":"blk-15196","spans":[{"id":"spn-14046","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.argument"},{"id":"spn-14047","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14048","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.vote"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-15197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14049","text":"But any MCP-compatible service can be a provider. The protocol is provider-agnostic by design."}]},{"id":"blk-15198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14050","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15199","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14051","text":"Contract Conformance Requirements"}]},{"id":"blk-15200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14052","text":"To satisfy a capability contract, a provider MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-15201","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14053","text":"1. Implement all declared operations"}]},{"id":"blk-15202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14054","text":"If the contract for "},{"id":"spn-14055","marks":["code"],"text":"&time.anomaly"},{"id":"spn-14056","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-14057","marks":["code"],"text":"detect"},{"id":"spn-14058","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14059","marks":["code"],"text":"enrich"},{"id":"spn-14060","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-14061","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-14062","text":" operations, the provider must implement all three."}]},{"id":"blk-15203","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14063","text":"2. Accept the declared input types"}]},{"id":"blk-15204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14064","text":"Each operation specifies an "},{"id":"spn-14065","marks":["code"],"text":"in"},{"id":"spn-14066","text":" type. The provider must accept data conforming to that type."}]},{"id":"blk-15205","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14067","text":"3. Produce the declared output types"}]},{"id":"blk-15206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14068","text":"Each operation specifies an "},{"id":"spn-14069","marks":["code"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-14070","text":" type. The provider must return data conforming to that type."}]},{"id":"blk-15207","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14071","text":"4. Respect accepts_from / feeds_into"}]},{"id":"blk-15208","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14072","text":"The provider must accept input from the types listed in "},{"id":"spn-14073","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-14074","text":" and produce output consumable by the types in "},{"id":"spn-14075","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-14076","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-15209","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14077","text":"5. Expose operations via MCP transport"}]},{"id":"blk-15210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14078","text":"Operations are invoked as MCP tools. The provider must respond to MCP tool calls over stdio or HTTP transport."}]},{"id":"blk-15211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14079","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15212","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14080","text":"MCP Transport Binding"}]},{"id":"blk-15213","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14081","text":"Providers expose their operations as MCP tools. The binding maps contract operations to MCP tool names:"}]},{"id":"blk-15214","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Contract operation    →    MCP tool name\n─────────────────────────────────────────\ndetect                →    detect_anomaly\nenrich                →    enrich_context\nlearn                 →    learn_observation"},{"id":"blk-15215","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14082","text":"Tool registration"}]},{"id":"blk-15216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14083","text":"When the provider starts as an MCP server, it registers tools that correspond to its contract operations:"}]},{"id":"blk-15217","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"detect_anomaly\",\n      \"description\": \"Detect anomalous events in temporal data streams.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"data\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"number\" } },\n          \"streams\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"data\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-15218","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14084","text":"Resource registration (optional)"}]},{"id":"blk-15219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14085","text":"Providers can also expose MCP resources for read-only state inspection:"}]},{"id":"blk-15220","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"resources\": [\n    {\n      \"uri\": \"provider://runtime/health\",\n      \"name\": \"Provider Health\",\n      \"description\": \"Runtime health status\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-15221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14086","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15222","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14087","text":"Provider Registration"}]},{"id":"blk-15223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14088","text":"To make a provider discoverable, register it in the capability registry."}]},{"id":"blk-15224","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14089","text":"Registry entry format"}]},{"id":"blk-15225","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"provider\": \"my-time-provider\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"capabilities\": [\"&time.anomaly\", \"&time.forecast\"],\n  \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n  \"command\": \"my-time-provider\",\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"contracts/v0.1.0/time.anomaly.contract.json\",\n    \"contracts/v0.1.0/time.forecast.contract.json\"\n  ],\n  \"homepage\": \"https://github.com/org/my-time-provider\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-15226","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14090","text":"The registry is used by "},{"id":"spn-14091","marks":["code"],"text":"provider: \"auto\""},{"id":"spn-14092","text":" resolution and by the "},{"id":"spn-14093","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-14094","text":" command to verify that providers exist."}]},{"id":"blk-15227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14095","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15228","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14096","text":"Testing Provider Conformance"}]},{"id":"blk-15229","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14097","text":"Contract validation"}]},{"id":"blk-15230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14098","text":"Verify that your provider's MCP tool surface matches the declared contract:"}]},{"id":"blk-15231","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"# List your provider's tools\necho '{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"tools/list\",\"id\":1}' | my-provider\n\n# Compare against the contract\nampersand validate-provider \\\n  --provider my-time-provider \\\n  --contract contracts/v0.1.0/time.anomaly.contract.json"},{"id":"blk-15232","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14099","text":"Integration testing"}]},{"id":"blk-15233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14100","text":"Test that each operation accepts the declared input type and produces the declared output type:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-15235","spans":[{"id":"spn-14101","text":"Test"}]},{"id":"blk-15236","spans":[{"id":"spn-14102","text":"What to verify"}]}],"id":"blk-15234","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-15237","spans":[{"id":"spn-14103","text":"Input acceptance"}]},{"id":"blk-15238","spans":[{"id":"spn-14104","text":"Send each "},{"id":"spn-14105","marks":["code"],"text":"in"},{"id":"spn-14106","text":" type; verify no error"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15239","spans":[{"id":"spn-14107","text":"Output shape"}]},{"id":"blk-15240","spans":[{"id":"spn-14108","text":"Verify output matches "},{"id":"spn-14109","marks":["code"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-14110","text":" type"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15241","spans":[{"id":"spn-14111","text":"Wildcard compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-15242","spans":[{"id":"spn-14112","text":"Send output from "},{"id":"spn-14113","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.*"},{"id":"spn-14114","text":" provider; verify acceptance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15243","spans":[{"id":"spn-14115","text":"Error handling"}]},{"id":"blk-15244","spans":[{"id":"spn-14116","text":"Send invalid input; verify graceful error response"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15245","spans":[{"id":"spn-14117","text":"Side effects"}]},{"id":"blk-15246","spans":[{"id":"spn-14118","text":"Verify "},{"id":"spn-14119","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: true"},{"id":"spn-14120","text":" operations modify state"}]}],[{"id":"blk-15247","spans":[{"id":"spn-14121","text":"Idempotency"}]},{"id":"blk-15248","spans":[{"id":"spn-14122","text":"Verify "},{"id":"spn-14123","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: false"},{"id":"spn-14124","text":" operations are safe to retry"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-15249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14125","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15250","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14126","text":"Common Implementation Patterns"}]},{"id":"blk-15251","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14127","text":"Pattern 1: Thin MCP wrapper"}]},{"id":"blk-15252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14128","text":"Wrap an existing service (database, API, ML model) in an MCP server that maps contract operations to service calls:"}]},{"id":"blk-15253","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"MCP tool call → Provider → Existing service → Response → MCP result"},{"id":"blk-15254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14129","text":"This is the simplest approach. Graphonomous wraps an Elixir/OTP application. A pgvector provider would wrap PostgreSQL."}]},{"id":"blk-15255","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14130","text":"Pattern 2: Multi-capability provider"}]},{"id":"blk-15256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14131","text":"A single provider can satisfy multiple contracts. Graphonomous provides "},{"id":"spn-14132","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.graph"},{"id":"spn-14133","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14134","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.episodic"},{"id":"spn-14135","text":", "},{"id":"spn-14136","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-14137","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-14138","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.attend"},{"id":"spn-14139","text":" — all from one MCP server."}]},{"id":"blk-15257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14140","text":"Register each capability separately in the contract, but serve them from one process."}]},{"id":"blk-15258","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14141","text":"Pattern 3: Stateless operation provider"}]},{"id":"blk-15259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14142","text":"Some capabilities are stateless — they transform input without maintaining state. These are simpler to implement and test:"}]},{"id":"blk-15260","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Input → Transform → Output (no state)"},{"id":"blk-15261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14143","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-14144","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic: true"},{"id":"spn-14145","text":" flag in the contract signals this pattern."}]},{"id":"blk-15262","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14146","text":"Pattern 4: Provider with feedback loop"}]},{"id":"blk-15263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14147","text":"Providers with "},{"id":"spn-14148","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-14149","text":" operations accept outcome feedback and improve over time. This requires persistent state:"}]},{"id":"blk-15264","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Input → Process → Output\n                  ↓\n          Feedback → State update"},{"id":"blk-15265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14150","text":"Mark these operations with "},{"id":"spn-14151","marks":["code"],"text":"side_effects: true"},{"id":"spn-14152","text":" in the contract."}]},{"id":"blk-15266","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14153","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-15267","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-14154","text":"Checklist: Shipping a New Provider"}]},{"id":"blk-15268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-14155","text":"1. Choose which capability contracts to satisfy 2. Implement all operations declared in each contract 3. Build an MCP server that exposes operations as tools 4. Write a registry entry for discoverability 5. Test conformance against the contract schemas 6. Publish the provider (npm, hex, crates.io, or standalone binary) 7. Submit a PR to add your provider to the registry"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierayr6up6tuihlv2z45tbxlrujt5lwgre6yqn27s7p6dsr2ieyf3bja","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}